    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "description": "Reading guide for this dashboard.",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**What this is.** Two pieces that make a hostname reachable from the LAN:\n- **MetalLB** (L2 mode) hands LoadBalancer Services an IP from pool `lan` = 192.168.68.240–245 (6 addresses) and answers **ARP** for\n  it from the node (speaker). Today: `gateway/public-istio` → .240, `gateway/mcp-istio` → .241.\n- **external-dns** watches HTTPRoutes and keeps Cloudflare **A records** (`<app>.staffops.space` → Gateway IP, not proxied) plus TXT\n  ownership records (`_extdns.` prefix, owner `k8s01`) in sync every minute (policy `sync`: it also deletes records of removed routes).\n\n**Healthy looks like:** pool usage 2/6, every LoadBalancer IP announced, config loaded and not stale, external-dns last successful sync\nunder ~2 minutes ago, source records = verified records, 0 errors.\n\n**When something goes red:** IP not announced / pool full → `kubectl --context k8s01 -n metallb-system logs ds/metallb-speaker`,\nfree an IP or grow the pool (`helm-charts/environment.yaml`); stale config → bad IPAddressPool/L2Advertisement; external-dns sync\nold or errors → Cloudflare token (Vault `homelab/cloudflare`) or API problem: `kubectl --context k8s01 -n external-dns logs deploy/external-dns`.\nNote: Cloudflare API calls are **not** instrumented by external-dns (only Kubernetes API calls are), so failures show up as soft errors\nand an old *last successful sync*. Details: `docs/dashboards/networking.md`."
      },
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 9
      }
    },
